// The processor's view of system memory: the agent that puts data into a block
// and the agent that checks a block's contents.
//
// It has no registers and no attributes, because memory is not a device here --
// it is storage the processor reaches with ordinary loads and stores. The
// component exists so that filling and checking are ACTIONS, schedulable
// alongside the transfers that move the data, rather than helper code somebody
// has to remember to call.
//
// The address space this component's actions allocate from is NOT declared
// here. A claim binds to the nearest matching space going up the component tree
// (§21.11.7), so system RAM belongs to the system -- see pss_top.
//
// The skeleton only (coding guidelines rule 3); the operations are in
// mem_c/functions/ and their scenario wrappers in mem_c/actions/.
component mem_c {
}
